  {
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "@ezhulenev do out-of-bounds indices need to be sorted and unique for XLA Scatter ops in `FILL_OR_DROP` mode to set `indices_are_sorted() && unique_indices()`?\r\n\r\nOn XLA:GPU `indices_are_sorted` appears to be unused as far as I can tell: [GitHub link](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Aopenxla%2Fxla%20path%3A%2F%5Exla%5C%2Fservice%5C%2Fgpu%5C%2F%2F%20indices_are_sorted&type=code). So the performance impact of having to set `indices_are_sorted=False` is none.\r\n\r\n... while `unique_indices` allows scatters to use non-atomic store instructions: [GitHub link](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Aopenxla%2Fxla+path%3A%2F%5Exla%5C%2Fservice%5C%2Fgpu%5C%2F%2F+unique_indices&type=code). So, it's important that we guarantee this with the `jnp.arange` trick.",
